+# Forklift cabin frames and expanded kits
+
+FKC01 replaces Side guards with Cabin frame. The posts, overhead rails and roof are replaced as one independent part, with tubular, pressed, twin-hoop, canted, rounded, cross-braced, canopy, lattice, arched, sport, grid, heavy-duty and safari designs. The original frame remains available. Lamps, mirrors, beacon, operator controls and lifting mast remain on the forklift. The Garage focuses on the upper cabin and places the preview callout there.
+
+FKC02 adds **ten further alternatives to each forklift category**: engine cover, rear guard, wheel covers and cabin frame. Each list now has fourteen choices: Original, three retained IDs and ten new IDs. This adds forty purchasable options. Old `body` IDs (`fork_rail`, `fork_plate`, `fork_twin`) now select cabin designs, retaining the same saved selection and ownership keys. Other vehicles' option tables and all unrelated backend catalogue entries are unchanged.
+
+FKC03 retains independent preview, compare, equip, reset, local save/reload, appearance sync, ownership confirmation, race and ghost construction. New items use the established 750-coin price. The server whitelist includes every option; matching backend deployment is required before new items can be purchased or synced online. No live service was changed.
+
+FKC04 refreshes four forklift base scenes, 104 full/simple kit scenes and its Garage template. These are original procedural assets, with no generated-image or third-party model input. Handling and collision contracts are unchanged. The shared build identity was regenerated by `dev.ps1`; it is excluded from the task-only checkpoint, and must be regenerated through that entry point after applying the patch.
+
+The [native review gallery](evidence/forklift-cabin-kits-2026-11-02/gallery.html) contains all 56 choices on each desktop renderer. Examples: [arched cabin](evidence/forklift-cabin-kits-2026-11-02/garage-gl-final/body-fork_arch.png), [canopy](evidence/forklift-cabin-kits-2026-11-02/garage-gl-final/body-fork_canopy.png), [turbine wheel cover](evidence/forklift-cabin-kits-2026-11-02/garage-gl-final/rims-fork_turbine.png), and [engine scoop](evidence/forklift-cabin-kits-2026-11-02/garage-gl-final/hood-fork_scoop.png). Final captures wait for both the kit sweep and camera transition to finish. Earlier captures are retained separately and can show the previous part during the sweep.
+
+R01 results on pinned Godot `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf`:
+
+| Check | Actual outcome |
+| --- | --- |
+| Every option, both detail levels, distinct geometry, retained mast/wheels/fixtures, original restoration | 741 checks, 0 failures |
+| Task-start Original body comparison, both detail levels | 6 checks, 0 failures; 127,864/40,072 matched triangles, zero unmatched geometry or UV/color and zero normal difference |
+| Prepared assets versus procedural construction, every option, both qualities | 1,580 checks, 0 failures |
+| Retained forklift model finish, solid surfaces, chain, forks and exhaust | 97 checks, 0 failures |
+| Actual Compatibility Garage, 56 previews, equip/reload, appearance round-trip, purchase cancellation, race and ghost | 187 checks, 0 failures; 56 final captures |
+| Actual desktop Mobile/Vulkan Garage, same workflow | 187 checks, 0 failures; 56 final captures |
+| Forklift, Electric and Hovercraft backend catalogue/ownership/purchase tests, PostgreSQL excluded | 171 passed, 6 deselected |
+| Retained economy, appearance sync and rivalry appearance tests | 40 passed, 1 skipped, 1 existing sticker-catalogue failure, 35 deselected |
+
+The retained sticker failure compares 25 server entries against 13 native entries. Its server list is byte-equivalent as parsed JSON before and after this task. The first backend run lacked `PYTHONPATH`; the next included three unavailable localhost PostgreSQL fixtures. Corrected final commands set the backend import path and explicitly exclude PostgreSQL. No PostgreSQL pass is claimed.
+
+Initial sandboxed Godot commands were denied access to the normal user log directory and Windows certificate store. Completed offline checks used isolated test `APPDATA` and normal Windows process access, with crash-dialog suppression. The first new assertion assumed Godot retained duplicate mesh names (741 checks, 2 failures); checking presence instead gives 741/0. The first Original comparison mixed a batched car with an unbatched legacy body (6 checks, 5 failures). Comparing both raw constructors gives 6/0 without relaxing the geometry, UV or normal requirements. These logs remain in the evidence directory.
+
+Actual reproduction commands, from the repository root:
+
+```powershell
+python scripts/run_no_crash_dialog.py -- powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/run_forklift_cabin_checks.ps1 -Stage geometry
+python scripts/run_no_crash_dialog.py -- powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/run_forklift_cabin_checks.ps1 -Stage original
+python scripts/run_no_crash_dialog.py -- powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/run_forklift_cabin_checks.ps1 -Stage bake
+python scripts/run_no_crash_dialog.py -- powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/run_forklift_cabin_checks.ps1 -Stage gl
+python scripts/run_no_crash_dialog.py -- powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/run_forklift_cabin_checks.ps1 -Stage mobile
+$env:PYTHONPATH='backend'
+.tools/backend-secure-venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest backend/tests/test_forklift_kits.py backend/tests/test_electric_kits.py backend/tests/test_hovercraft_kits.py -k 'not postgres' -q --disable-warnings
+.tools/backend-secure-venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest backend/tests/test_earned_coins.py backend/tests/test_appearance_sync.py backend/tests/test_rivalry_appearance.py -k 'not postgres' -q --disable-warnings
+python docs/evidence/forklift-cabin-kits-2026-11-02/finalize.py
+python docs/evidence/forklift-cabin-kits-2026-11-02/checkpoint.py
+```
+
+The initial `geometry` stage stopped at the mismatched comparison. The corrected comparison ran separately; the retained model regression ran after Mobile and passed 97 checks. Existing legacy-test metrics were backed up, the new output was archived here, and the exact historical metrics were restored. The runner now supplies this task's evidence directory explicitly.
+
+Changed runtime sources are `forklift_model.gd`, `forklift_kits.gd`, the forklift section of `vehicle_customisation.gd`, `garage_customisation_camera.gd`, `garage_part_indicator.gd` and the forklift server catalogue. Supporting changes cover the two existing forklift tests, original/prepared comparison fixtures, backend purchase cases, the deterministic catalogue authoring helper and isolated runner. [report.json](evidence/forklift-cabin-kits-2026-11-02/report.json) records source/asset/image hashes. Q01's [task-only binary patch](evidence/forklift-cabin-kits-2026-11-02/task.patch) is checked forward/reverse and compared byte-for-byte in an owned temporary Git repository; [checkpoint.json](evidence/forklift-cabin-kits-2026-11-02/checkpoint.json) records the result. The main Git index is not written.
+
+The checkpoint baseline retains concurrent documentation additions and uses repository LF line endings for the server JSON. Other task-start source and binary snapshots remain exact. This excludes other agents' Daily, Rivalry and loading-review notes from the patch.
+
+Owner appearance/touch acceptance, phone performance and matching online catalogue rollout remain. New display copy continues the existing forklift English fallback. No device query/test, APK, real purchase, owner-save change, owner-process restart, live sync mutation or deployment was performed. Concurrent work is preserved.
